//! RFC 3261 §7: a SIP message is a start line, then header fields, then an empty
//! line, then an optional body. §7.1 gives the Request-Line (method, Request-URI,
//! SIP-Version) and §7.2 the Status-Line (SIP-Version, Status-Code,
//! Reason-Phrase); §7.3 gives the header fields, which have the same shape as
//! HTTP's. Text, not a field table (DEVIATIONS T1).
//!
//! Generated by dev/protogen from dev/protogen/specs/sip.toml. Field layouts
//! come from the RFC cited above; edit the spec, not this file.

